cceptance records, no receipts. The `gate` pre-check reports evals execute cleanly at 0 pass / 4 fail per task, which is the expected shape for unbuilt work — those are the red tests waiting for implementation, not failures of the specs.\n\n## The distinction that matters here\n\nThe signed plan review is **not** a leaf seal. `batch` created these four leaves unsealed; `gate --stamp` would authorize a specific revision; `accept --stamp` would record verified acceptance. Right now the chain sits between the first and second of those, exactly where the review text says it should sit.\n\nPer your instruction I've left it there — no `gate --stamp`, no `mesh run`, no `executor`. The CLI's own suggested next command for each task is `gate --stamp <path>`; that remains unrun and needs your explicit go-ahead."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3026,"cache_read_input_tokens":24678,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3026},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"62bc3ee2-1378-4030-af79-fa0e0ab9d373","uuid":"0f51c3d7-4a1d-4ed4-9cfe-17ad905a14f2","timestamp":"2026-09-14T22:25:13.720Z","request_id":"req_011Cf47hANka2d5ohiJ7k44K"}
